The media driver builds for LikeOS.

The toolchain names this system by its own macro and undefines the other
one, and the driver's build had been defining that other one itself; it no
longer does.  Its bundled copies of the kernel interface headers get a
branch for this system (the standard integer types and the ioctl encoding
from the C library), the two guards that chose the POSIX flavour accept
LikeOS, and the decoder's look at the framebuffer for a default display
size reads the C library's framebuffer header.  A thread's identifier
is a pointer here, so the number the driver makes of it goes through an
integer of the pointer's size.  The bundled copy of the device
enumeration code takes the paths of the first kind of system, since this
kernel serves the same device and bus directories.

